{"text": " You wake up in 1500 in London. It's still dark. Next door a hammer is already going and the street smells of wet straw and wood smoke. Did you know that historians estimate only about one woman in 100 in England could even write her own name? So what is school to you? Something for other people. For priests and rich boys. Most children learn by working. If you're a craftsman's son, you're a apprentice. Usually seven years living in your master's house, learning his trade by doing it. If you're lucky enough for grammar school, lessons often start at six in the morning. In Latin, and if you're a prince, nine-year-old prince Henry, the future Henry, the eighth, has a teacher all to himself, the poet John Skeleton. One teacher, one child, remember that. In 1524, a rebel preacher, Martin Luther writes to the leaders of German cities. Build schools, he says, for boys and for girls. Partly so everyone can read the Bible. Why would a whole town care if a farmer's daughter can read? Soon a colony across the ocean will write it into law.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.88, "text": " You wake up in 1500 in London.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 22671, 294, 7042, 13, 50494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12323065461783574, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 0.011147940531373024, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.12, "probability": 0.6786381602287292}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.28, "probability": 0.9938552975654602}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.28, "end": 0.46, "probability": 0.9993879795074463}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.46, "end": 0.58, "probability": 0.9884887337684631}, {"word": " 1500", "start": 0.58, "end": 0.98, "probability": 0.6506542563438416}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.98, "end": 1.64, "probability": 0.9556434750556946}, {"word": " London.", "start": 1.64, "end": 1.88, "probability": 0.9962989687919617}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 2.32, "end": 3.24, "text": " It's st